WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.909
Abdominal illness can look similar across immune,

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:07.131
inflammatory and infectious processes. Clinical

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:09.667
appearance alone may be insufficient.

00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:17.492
Diagnostic interpretation can involve biomarkers,

00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:21.318
endoscopy and tissue findings, with different roles

00:00:21.318 --> 00:00:21.543
and

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:23.973
limitations in distinct diseases.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:32.177
Part Two surveys emerging diagnostic techniques and

00:00:32.177 --> 00:00:36.059
treatments for autoimmune gastrointestinal conditions

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:36.206
in

00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:38.364
a changing evidence landscape.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.509
Therapeutic approaches follow disease mechanisms, but

00:00:46.509 --> 00:00:50.243
treatment evidence differs by condition, study design

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:50.454
and

00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:51.768
patient population.

00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:59.527
A new assay or biologic may improve the available

00:00:59.527 --> 00:01:00.048
choices

00:01:00.048 --> 00:01:03.544
without solving every diagnostic or therapeutic

00:01:03.544 --> 00:01:04.213
question.

00:01:08.092 --> 00:01:12.221
The 2022 chapter documents the literature available

00:01:12.221 --> 00:01:12.626
then.

00:01:12.626 --> 00:01:16.603
Current medical decisions require updated clinical

00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:19.546
evidence and professional evaluation.
